// Copy to LocalSigning.xcconfig and fill in. That file is git-ignored.
//
// A free Apple account ("personal team") can sign this app, but it cannot use
// identifiers registered to someone else -- an App ID and an app group are
// globally unique and belong to whoever registered them first. Omi's are
// already taken, so a personal build needs its own. No amount of paying Apple
// changes that; the $99 membership buys a one-year provisioning profile
// instead of a seven-day one, not someone else's identifiers.
//
// Find your team id in Xcode > Settings > Accounts, or run:
//   security find-identity -p codesigning -v
// and read the OU= field of the certificate's subject.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=XXXXXXXXXX
